# Evaluation Instructions

First determine whether the overall criterion is applicable.

If it is not applicable, return:
- applicable = false
- all subcriteria results = null

If it is applicable, evaluate EACH subcriterion independently. Within each
subcriterion judge EVERY rule listed above, one rule at a time:

- report the rules in order using the `index` field, starting from 0; the
  rule count must exactly match the list above;

- set `passed` to true only when the trajectory contains concrete,
  observable evidence that the rule is satisfied; set it to false otherwise.
  A rule that states its own applicability condition (e.g. "when the problem
  involves X ...") is passed when the condition does not apply to this
  trajectory;

- do not infer actions or reasoning that are not supported by the trajectory;

- derive the subcriterion `score` by dividing the number of passed rules by
  the total number of rules, rounded to two decimal places. Fewer satisfied
  rules always means a lower score: no rule passes gives 0, half of the rules
  gives about 0.5, all rules pass gives 1;

- write the subcriterion `reasoning`: one concise paragraph that justifies
  the score by summarising which rules passed, which failed, and on which
  trajectory evidence the verdicts rest.


